Third-party data
----------------

The table of Simplified and Traditional Chinese characters
(core/common/src/main/java/com/vpr/screenlate/core/common/language/ChineseScriptTable.kt), generated by
scripts/chinese-scripts/build.py, is derived from:
  the Unihan database (https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/), Copyright © 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc.,
  Unicode License V3 (its text is at the end of this file);
  CC-CEDICT (https://cc-cedict.org/wiki/), CC BY-SA 4.0, by MDBG and the CC-CEDICT contributors, in the
  Yomitan conversion by cc-cedict-yomitan (https://github.com/MarvNC/cc-cedict-yomitan).
  The table is shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.

The Hanja dictionary (dictionary/api/src/main/assets/catalog/unihan-hanja.zip), generated by
scripts/hanja/unihan_hanja.py and installed with Korean, is derived from the Unihan database
(https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/), Copyright © 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc., Unicode License V3.

Dictionaries offered for download are not part of the APK; each one carries its own license and
attribution, shown in the app under Dictionaries. The frequency dictionaries that the app builds on the device
(and scripts/frequency on a computer) use the word lists of wordfreq (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq) by
Robyn Speer, data licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, which come from Wikipedia, OpenSubtitles, SUBTLEX, Google Books Ngrams
and other sources; each built dictionary names them all and is shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.

Fonts offered for download in the Popup settings (Japanese, Chinese, Korean, Hindi and Latin, from the Google Fonts
repository, https://github.com/google/fonts) are not part of the APK either; each is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1,
shown in the app with its source.

